      "seed": 2134065106,
      "version": 1117,
      "versionNonce": 1671471758,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786179040817,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Allows an object to pass a request along a chain of potential\nhandlers, each handler in the chain decides either to process\nthe request or pass it to the next handler\n\nCOR is sort of like linkedlist, but in linked list all the classes\nare the same, while in COR the classes are all subclasses but\nare technically different classes.\n\nUseCases:\n \n1) Logger (Info -> Debug -> Error) \n2) Design a leave request system",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Allows an object to pass a request along a chain of potential handlers, each handler in the chain decides either to process the request or pass it to the next handler\n\nCOR is sort of like linkedlist, but in linked list all the classes are the same, while in COR the classes are all subclasses but are technically different classes.\n\nUseCases:\n \n1) Logger (Info -> Debug -> Error) \n2) Design a leave request system",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
